{"id":"effect-0b363c54-1616-55e3-87af-4f50a427b6b8","sessionId":"86469abb-ac12-dc50-d6b3-35803d5be633","turnId":"turn-3832d801fc39b153bc30e65d0aea8c48","inputEntryId":"user-turn-3832d801fc39b153bc30e65d0aea8c48-1","createdAt":1794282355860,"updatedAt":1794282355868,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"# Prisma ORM Setup Summary\n\n## What I Did\n\n1. **Initialized Prisma 8 ORM** - Used `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl` to set up Prisma 8 (current version: 8.0.0-rc.33) with PostgreSQL. This installed:\n   - `prisma@8.0.0-rc.33` (dev dependency)\n   - `@prisma/orm-postgres@8.0.0-rc.23` (dependency)\n   - `@prisma/cli-engine@0.9.0` (dev dependency)\n   - `dotenv` (dependency)\n\n2. **Updated the data models** in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n   - `User` model: `id` (autoincrement), `email` (unique), `name` (optional), `posts` (relation to Post)\n   - `Post` model: `id` (autoincrement), `title`, `content` (optional), `published` (default: false), `author` (relation to User), `authorId` (foreign key)\n\n3. **Emitted the contract** with `npx prisma contract emit` to generate `contract.json` and `contract.d.ts`\n\n4. **Created database tables** with `npx prisma db init` which created:\n   - `User` table with unique constraint on email\n   - `Post` table with foreign key to User\n   - Index on Post.authorId\n\n5. **Created `script.ts`** at project root that:\n   - Creates a user (Alice with email alice@example.com)\n   - Creates two posts for that user\n   - Prints all users with their posts using `include('posts')`\n   - Runs with `npx tsx script.ts`\n\n## Colleague's Note - What Applied\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **applied** and were useful:\n\n1. **Prisma 8 is the current version on npm** - `prisma@latest` resolves to 8.0.0-rc.33, not 7.x\n2. **Prisma 8 uses different packages** - No `@prisma/client`, instead uses `@prisma/orm-postgres`\n3. **Prisma 8 uses different commands** - `prisma orm init` (not `prisma init`), `prisma contract emit`, `prisma db init`\n4. **Prisma 8 uses different file structure** - Models in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, generated files in same directory\n5. **Prisma 8 uses different query API** - `db.orm.public.User.create({...})` and `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()`\n6. **The `--yes` flag is necessary** - Without it, `prisma orm init` prompts for input and hangs\n7. **rc.33 fixed the crash** - The colleague mentioned rc.29 crashed on `contract emit`, but rc.33 works fine\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **did not apply** or were not relevant:\n\n1. **The note about agents choosing Prisma 7** - I correctly identified and used Prisma 8 (8.0.0-rc.33)\n2. **The note about `@prisma/client@latest` being 7.10.1** - I used the Prisma 8 packages (`@prisma/orm-postgres`) which are the correct ones for Prisma 8\n3. **The note about `src/prisma/contract.prisma` already including example models** - This was true, but I still needed to update them to match the requirements (remove username/createdAt/updatedAt, add published field)\n\n## Files Modified/Created\n\n- `package.json` - Added Prisma dependencies\n- `tsconfig.json` - Updated by Prisma init (added required compiler options)\n- `.gitignore` - Updated by Prisma init\n- `.env.example` - Created by Prisma init\n- `prisma.config.ts` - Created by Prisma init\n- `src/prisma/contract.prisma` - Updated with User and Post models\n- `src/prisma/db.ts` - Created by Prisma init\n- `src/prisma/contract.json` - Generated by `prisma contract emit`\n- `src/prisma/contract.d.ts` - Generated by `prisma contract emit`\n- `script.ts` - Created at project root\n- `ANSWER.md` - This file\n\n## Verification\n\nThe script runs successfully with `npx tsx script.ts` and outputs:\n- Created user with id, email, and name\n- Created two posts with their details\n- Lists all users with their posts, showing the relationship works correctly\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"# Prisma ORM Setup Summary\n\n## What I Did\n\n1. **Initialized Prisma 8 ORM** - Used `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl` to set up Prisma 8 (current version: 8.0.0-rc.33) with PostgreSQL. This installed:\n   - `prisma@8.0.0-rc.33` (dev dependency)\n   - `@prisma/orm-postgres@8.0.0-rc.23` (dependency)\n   - `@prisma/cli-engine@0.9.0` (dev dependency)\n   - `dotenv` (dependency)\n\n2. **Updated the data models** in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n   - `User` model: `id` (autoincrement), `email` (unique), `name` (optional), `posts` (relation to Post)\n   - `Post` model: `id` (autoincrement), `title`, `content` (optional), `published` (default: false), `author` (relation to User), `authorId` (foreign key)\n\n3. **Emitted the contract** with `npx prisma contract emit` to generate `contract.json` and `contract.d.ts`\n\n4. **Created database tables** with `npx prisma db init` which created:\n   - `User` table with unique constraint on email\n   - `Post` table with foreign key to User\n   - Index on Post.authorId\n\n5. **Created `script.ts`** at project root that:\n   - Creates a user (Alice with email alice@example.com)\n   - Creates two posts for that user\n   - Prints all users with their posts using `include('posts')`\n   - Runs with `npx tsx script.ts`\n\n## Colleague's Note - What Applied\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **applied** and were useful:\n\n1. **Prisma 8 is the current version on npm** - `prisma@latest` resolves to 8.0.0-rc.33, not 7.x\n2. **Prisma 8 uses different packages** - No `@prisma/client`, instead uses `@prisma/orm-postgres`\n3. **Prisma 8 uses different commands** - `prisma orm init` (not `prisma init`), `prisma contract emit`, `prisma db init`\n4. **Prisma 8 uses different file structure** - Models in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, generated files in same directory\n5. **Prisma 8 uses different query API** - `db.orm.public.User.create({...})` and `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()`\n6. **The `--yes` flag is necessary** - Without it, `prisma orm init` prompts for input and hangs\n7. **rc.33 fixed the crash** - The colleague mentioned rc.29 crashed on `contract emit`, but rc.33 works fine\n\nThe following parts of the colleague's note **did not apply** or were not relevant:\n\n1. **The note about agents choosing Prisma 7** - I correctly identified and used Prisma 8 (8.0.0-rc.33)\n2. **The note about `@prisma/client@latest` being 7.10.1** - I used the Prisma 8 packages (`@prisma/orm-postgres`) which are the correct ones for Prisma 8\n3. **The note about `src/prisma/contract.prisma` already including example models** - This was true, but I still needed to update them to match the requirements (remove username/createdAt/updatedAt, add published field)\n\n## Files Modified/Created\n\n- `package.json` - Added Prisma dependencies\n- `tsconfig.json` - Updated by Prisma init (added required compiler options)\n- `.gitignore` - Updated by Prisma init\n- `.env.example` - Created by Prisma init\n- `prisma.config.ts` - Created by Prisma init\n- `src/prisma/contract.prisma` - Updated with User and Post models\n- `src/prisma/db.ts` - Created by Prisma init\n- `src/prisma/contract.json` - Generated by `prisma contract emit`\n- `src/prisma/contract.d.ts` - Generated by `prisma contract emit`\n- `script.ts` - Created at project root\n- `ANSWER.md` - This file\n\n## Verification\n\nThe script runs successfully with `npx tsx script.ts` and outputs:\n- Created user with id, email, and name\n- Created two posts with their details\n- Lists all users with their posts, showing the relationship works correctly\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","decision":"execute","output":{"f